G('pvalue', 'p-value / FDR / q-value', ['FDR', 'p-value', 'q-value'], 'False discovery rate', 'A p-value is the chance of a result at least this extreme if nothing is going on. When many pathways are tested some look significant by chance, so p-values are corrected (Benjamini–Hochberg). The corrected value is the FDR or q-value. q < 0.05 is the usual limit.', 'network', ['network', 'project'])
